{
  "sn7.1:0.1": "Linked Discourses 7.1 ",
  "sn7.1:0.2": "1. The Perfected Ones ",
  "sn7.1:0.3": "With Dhanañjānī ",
  "sn7.1:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn7.1:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. ",
  "sn7.1:1.3": "Now at that time the wife of a certain brahmin of the Bhāradvāja clan, a brahmin lady named Dhanañjānī, was devoted to the Buddha, the teaching, and the Saṅgha. ",
  "sn7.1:1.4": "Once, while she was bringing her husband his meal, she tripped and expressed this heartfelt sentiment three times: ",
  "sn7.1:2.1": "“Homage to him, the blessed one, the perfected one, the fully awakened Buddha! ",
  "sn7.1:3.1": "Homage to him, the blessed one, the perfected one, the fully awakened Buddha! ",
  "sn7.1:4.1": "Homage to him, the blessed one, the perfected one, the fully awakened Buddha!” ",
  "sn7.1:5.1": "When she said this, the brahmin said to Dhanañjānī: ",
  "sn7.1:5.2": "“That’d be right. For the slightest thing this lowlife woman praises that shaven ascetic. ",
  "sn7.1:5.3": "Right now, lowlife woman, I’m going to refute your teacher’s doctrine!” ",
  "sn7.1:5.4": "“Brahmin, I don’t see anyone in this world—with its gods, Māras, and divinities, this population with its ascetics and brahmins, its gods and humans—who can refute the doctrine of the Blessed One, the perfected one, the fully awakened Buddha. ",
  "sn7.1:5.5": "But anyway, you should go. When you’ve gone you’ll understand.